  "body": "Add a connectedness member to MutationObserverInit. When it is true,\nthe observer gets a \"connected\" or \"disconnected\" record each time the\ntarget becomes connected or stops being connected, including when that\nhappens because an ancestor or shadow host is inserted or removed. The\nsubtree member does not apply to connectedness, as that would require\na record for each node of an inserted or removed subtree.\n\nThese records are queued where the connectedCallback and\ndisconnectedCallback custom element reactions are enqueued. That puts\nthem before the tree mutation record for the insertion or removal that\ncaused them, also when that record is queued later, such as for\nreplaceChildren(). The move algorithm does not queue them as it cannot\nchange whether a node is connected.\n\nAs this makes it natural to observe many individual nodes with a\nsingle MutationObserver object, also add unobserve(target), which\nstops observing target as requested through observe() without\naffecting other targets. Unlike disconnect(), it does not empty the\nrecord queue, as a record can be the result of multiple registered\nobservers. This matches IntersectionObserver's unobserve().\n\nFixes #126. Fixes #533.\n\nTests: https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/63396\n\n- [ ] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * WebKit\n   * …\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/63396\n- [ ] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: …\n   * Gecko: …\n   * WebKit: …\n- [ ] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: …\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use.\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/dom/1508.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 9, 2026, 2:12 PM UTC (811f16d)\">Preview</a> | <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/dom/1508/3071e5f...811f16d.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 9, 2026, 2:12 PM UTC (811f16d)\">Diff</a>",
